    "faq": [
      {
        "question": "Does this skill connect to DNAnexus automatically?",
        "answer": "No. It provides guidance and examples; execution requires local tools, authentication, identifiers, permissions, and user-approved commands."
      },
      {
        "question": "Which DNAnexus interfaces does it cover?",
        "answer": "It covers the dx command line, the dxpy Python SDK, app and applet configuration, data objects, jobs, and workflows."
      },
      {
        "question": "Can it handle FASTQ, BAM, and VCF workflows?",
        "answer": "Yes. The patterns apply to common genomics files, but each tool, schema, resource setting, and validation rule requires project-specific adaptation."
      },
      {
        "question": "Does it create or store credentials?",
        "answer": "No. Use DNAnexus login or an approved secret manager, and never include real tokens in prompts or generated source files."
      },
      {
        "question": "Can it manage production data?",
        "answer": "It can guide production operations. Verify identifiers, permissions, retention requirements, and backups before modifying, moving, archiving, or deleting data."
      },
